// Who someone is and what they may do. Identity comes from Authentik;
// authority is derived from these tables and never from the session.
// See lib/domain/permissions.ts and lib/server/capabilities.ts.

// One thing a role may be allowed to do. The editable half of authority: which
// roles hold which of these is a table (RoleCapability), maintained in
// Inställningar → Roller.
//
// The list itself is not editable, and cannot be: a capability is a name a call
// site asks about, so one nobody checks would be a tickbox that does nothing.
// Every value here has exactly one helper in lib/domain/permissions.ts, and
// that is the whole of the contract.
//
// What is deliberately NOT in here is the attest rule. Whether you may attest
// one particular allocation depends on whose utlägg it is, what the submitter
// holds, and whether the cost centre falls under a result unit you answer for.
// See canAttestAllocation. That is not a permission a role has, it is a
// question about two people and a row, and a tickbox claiming to grant it would
// be a tickbox that lies. ATTEST_VIEW below grants sight of the attest queue,
// which is what `hasAttestRole` has always meant.
enum Capability {
  /// Full authority over other people's utlägg: attest any of them, edit any
  /// of them. Woven into the attest rule and its query, not merely a page.
  ADMIN
  /// Bokföring: see every utlägg, book vouchers, return a wrongly-approved one.
  BOOKKEEPING
  /// Books in Fortnox under their own login (drives the status on /profile).
  FORTNOX_LOGIN
  /// Mark an exported utlägg as no longer exported.
  EXPORT_UNDO
  /// Reach Inställningar. At least one live person must always hold this. See
  /// lib/server/capabilities.ts.
  SETTINGS
  /// Read the stock overview and the log.
  STOCK_VIEW
  /// Register movements, run an event, close a stocktake.
  STOCK_MANAGE
  /// See the budget pages.
  BUDGET_VIEW
  /// Comment on a budget account.
  BUDGET_COMMENT
  /// Lock an adopted budget, and unlock it.
  BUDGET_LOCK
  /// Record a budgetavsteg or budgetförflyttning on a locked budget.
  BUDGET_CHANGE_LOCKED
  /// See the attest queue. Whether any single utlägg in it can actually be
  /// attested is still canAttestAllocation's answer, per row.
  ATTEST_VIEW
  /// Read the avtal archive and open the documents in it.
  CONTRACT_VIEW
  /// Put a contract in the archive, draw an uthyrningsavtal, edit the gear
  /// catalogue. Deliberately not the same as being allowed to bind the
  /// section: who may sign for it is a question about firmateckning, and the
  /// answer is FIRMATECKNARE below.
  CONTRACT_MANAGE
  /// Grant one late eget utlägg a dispens, so it may be filed after the
  /// 60-day deadline has passed. Per claim, with a reason, before it goes for
  /// attest. Held by the skattmästare alone by default, the way BUDGET_LOCK
  /// and BUDGET_CHANGE_LOCKED are: departing from a rule the section set is
  /// the same kind of act as sealing the figures it set. See
  /// canWaiveFilingDeadline in lib/domain/permissions.ts.
  EXPENSE_DEADLINE_WAIVE
  /// May be named as the section's signatory on a contract.
  ///
  /// Firmateckning is a fact about the section's stadgar rather than a
  /// permission this app grants, and this row does not confer it. What it does
  /// is record who holds it, so the rental form can offer those people and only
  /// those people. Held by ordförande and skattmästare, which means a handover
  /// in Authentik is a handover here with nothing to remember.
  ///
  /// It opens nothing. Somebody holding this and nothing else can be named on a
  /// contract and cannot open the archive it is filed in. That is the whole
  /// point of it being separate from CONTRACT_MANAGE: the uthyrningsansvarig
  /// who draws a contract is usually not the person who signs it.
  FIRMATECKNARE
  /// Read uthyrningsavtal, and nothing else in the archive.
  ///
  /// The narrow half of CONTRACT_VIEW. Somebody running uthyrningen needs to
  /// find last spring's rental and has no business reading what the section
  /// pays a sponsor. Which contracts that leaves reachable is one filter in
  /// lib/data/contract-scope.ts, applied by every query and every route.
  RENTAL_VIEW
  /// Draw an uthyrningsavtal and keep the gear catalogue.
  ///
  /// The narrow half of CONTRACT_MANAGE, and it can only ever touch a contract
  /// whose kind is RENTAL. A holder of this cannot file a sponsoravtal, edit
  /// one, or delete one.
  RENTAL_MANAGE
  /// Send a reminder about an utlägg to whoever it is waiting on: its
  /// attesters, or the submitter. From the utlägg itself, or several at once
  /// from the list. Held by the admins by default.
  SEND_REMINDERS
}

// Section role. A user may hold several (e.g. skattförman + resultatansvarig),
// so it's stored as an array. Access and attest authority are derived from the
// set of roles in lib/permissions.ts, never from a single value.
//   SKATTMASTARE / ORDFORANDE       admins; full access; attest any expense but their own
//   VICE_SKATTMASTARE               bookkeeping; attest expenses by "ordinarie" submitters
//   SKATTFORMAN                     bookkeeping (book + return wrongly-approved)
//   RESULTATANSVARIG                attest/handle expenses for the result unit(s) they answer for
//   ORDINARIE                       regular functionary; submits own expenses
enum Role {
  SKATTMASTARE
  ORDFORANDE
  VICE_SKATTMASTARE
  SKATTFORMAN
  RESULTATANSVARIG
  // Runs the bar's stock. Deliberately outside the treasury roles: keeping the
  // lagerbokföring is not bookkeeping, and the people who do it are not the
  // people who book vouchers. See canManageStock in lib/domain/permissions.ts.
  STOCKARE
  // Runs uthyrningen. Outside the treasury roles for the same reason STOCKARE
  // is: letting out the section's gear is not bookkeeping, and what this role
  // reaches is uthyrningsavtal and the gear catalogue, not the avtal archive.
  // A sponsoravtal's terms are none of its business. See contract-scope.ts.
  UTHYRNINGSANSVARIG
  ORDINARIE
}

model User {
  id String @id @default(cuid())

  // Authentik's `preferred_username`, the LTH student id ("lu1234ge-s"), and
  // the identity this app is keyed on. It is the one thing about a member that
  // does not change: an email address can be re-pointed and a name can be
  // changed, and neither should make somebody a different person here. Same
  // key the guild's own web app uses (Member.studentId), so a future
  // integration has something to join on.
  studentId String @unique

  // Descriptive, not identifying. Refreshed from Authentik on each sign-in.
  email String @unique
  name  String

  // Derived from the Authentik group list at sign-in, and only there
  // (lib/server/authentik-roles.ts), which is why a session lasts a day. See
  // `session` in src/auth.ts. Authority is still read from this column and
  // never from the token, see lib/server/current-user.ts.
  roles Role[] @default([ORDINARIE]) // one or more section roles; authority derived in lib/permissions.ts

  // The result units this person answers for, by ResultUnit.name, derived
  // from the same group list, in the same place, at the same moment as
  // `roles`. Names rather than ids because the mapping is written against the
  // section's vocabulary (lib/server/authentik-roles.ts) and a cuid means
  // nothing there; a name with no row behind it simply grants nothing, which
  // the settings screen reports.
  resultUnits String[] @default([])

  // The Authentik group list as it stood at this person's last sign-in.
  //
  // Not authority. `roles` and `resultUnits` above are, and they are what every
  // gate reads. This is the evidence they were derived from, kept so the
  // derivation can be run again without the person being here: change the
  // mapping in Inställningar → Roller and everyone it touches is recomputed on
  // the spot, rather than one by one over the next day as they happen to sign
  // in. It is also the only way the settings screen can say what a change is
  // about to do, and the only way a mapping written against a group nobody
  // holds (a typo, silent by design) can be pointed at.
  authentikGroups String[] @default([])

  // Bank details for REIMBURSEMENT payouts (Swedish clearing + account no.)
  bankClearingNumber String?
  bankAccountNumber  String?

  active Boolean @default(true)

  submittedExpenses    Expense[]                @relation("ExpenseSubmitter")
  allocationApprovals  ExpenseCostAllocation[]  @relation("AllocationApprover")
  uploadedReceipts     Receipt[]                @relation("ReceiptUploader")
  events               ExpenseEvent[]           @relation("EventActor")
  deadlineWaivers      Expense[]                @relation("ExpenseDeadlineWaiver")
  createdVerifications Verification[]           @relation("VerificationCreator")
  heldCards            Card[]                   @relation("CardHolder")
  budgets              Budget[]                 @relation("BudgetAuthor")
  lockedBudgets        Budget[]                 @relation("BudgetLocker")
  budgetComments       BudgetComment[]          @relation("BudgetCommentAuthor")
  budgetChanges        BudgetChange[]           @relation("BudgetChangeAuthor")
  revokedBudgetChanges BudgetChange[]           @relation("BudgetChangeRevoker")
  fortnoxConnections   FortnoxConnection[]      @relation("FortnoxConnector")
  fortnoxSession       FortnoxUserSession?      @relation("FortnoxUserSession")
  incomeBatches        IncomeBatch[]            @relation("IncomeBatchCreator")
  stockEntries         StockEntry[]             @relation("StockEntryActor")
  stockEvents          StockEvent[]             @relation("StockEventCreator")
  stockChanges         StockChange[]            @relation("StockChangeActor")
  stockProductChanges  StockProductChange[]     @relation("StockProductChangeActor")
  mileageRates         MileageRate[]            @relation("MileageRateAuthor")
  contracts            Contract[]               @relation("ContractCreator")
  contractFiles        ContractFile[]           @relation("ContractFileUploader")
  rentalChecks         RentalDetails[]          @relation("RentalChecker")
  counterparties       Counterparty[]           @relation("CounterpartyCreator")
  outboundEmails       OutboundEmail[]          @relation("EmailRecipient")
  sentTestEmails       OutboundEmail[]          @relation("EmailSender")
  notificationPrefs    NotificationPreference[]
  expensePresence      ExpensePresence[]        @relation("ExpensePresenceUser")
  exportClaims         Expense[]                @relation("ExpenseExportClaim")

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  // ── Indexes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // The three array columns are all queried by containment, not by value:
  // `roles hasSome` behind every capability check (lib/server/capabilities.ts),
  // `resultUnits has` when a result unit is deleted or renamed, and
  // `authentikGroups isEmpty` on the settings screen. Postgres answers those
  // with `&&` and `@>`, which a btree cannot serve at all, so without these
  // each one is a sequential scan of the whole member table.
  //
  // Harmless at the section's current size and not a thing to discover later:
  // the capability lookup is on the request path for every gated page in the
  // app, so it is the one that stops being free first.
  @@index([roles], type: Gin)
  @@index([resultUnits], type: Gin)
  @@index([authentikGroups], type: Gin)
}

// ── Authority ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Two tables and one rule: an Authentik group confers roles and result units
// (GroupRole, GroupResultUnit), and a role confers capabilities
// (RoleCapability). Everything the app asks about authority resolves through
// these. See lib/server/authentik-roles.ts for the first half and
// lib/server/capabilities.ts for the second.
//
// The rows used to be three tables in lib/server/authentik-roles.ts, deployed.
// They are data now because the section edits them: a committee is renamed, a
// unit is handed to someone who is not its head, a role is given the run of a
// page it did not have. What is NOT data is the Role and Capability enums
// themselves. Those are names the code says out loud, and a row naming one
// that does not exist would be a grant nothing can honour.

/// An Authentik group, and a role holding it confers. Several rows per group.
model GroupRole {
  /// Lowercased, exactly as Authentik writes it: "dsek.sex.mastare".
  group String
  role  Role

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  @@id([group, role])
  @@index([group])
}

/// An Authentik group, and a result unit holding it makes you answer for.
///
/// A row here also confers RESULTATANSVARIG. The role and the reach come from
/// the same line, so neither can be granted without the other
/// (lib/server/authentik-roles.ts).
model GroupResultUnit {
  group        String
  resultUnitId String
  /// Cascades: a result unit that no longer exists cannot be answered for, and
  /// leaving the row would be an ownership pointing at nothing. This is the
  /// whole reason the mapping is a foreign key and not a name. It used to be a
  /// name, and a typo in it granted silently nothing.
  resultUnit   ResultUnit @relation(fields: [resultUnitId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  @@id([group, resultUnitId])
  @@index([group])
  @@index([resultUnitId])
}

/// A role, and one thing it is allowed to do.
model RoleCapability {
  role       Role
  capability Capability

  createdAt DateTime @default(now())

  @@id([role, capability])
  @@index([role])
}
